# Hook ignore

Copyright (c) 2026 Devrecated.

Local kill-switch: `.cursor/hooks/hookignore.yaml` (gitignored). Missing file = every hook on. Example: `.cursor/hooks/hookignore.example.yaml`.

If the user is upset about a hook (nags, wrong ticket, worktree footer, shell deny, leftover session):

1. Ask whether they want it added to `hookignore.yaml`.
2. If yes and the file is missing, copy the example, then set that hook to `false` or add its name under `ignore:`.
3. Name the hook from the script basename (`ticket-progress-files`, `worktree-status`, `session-end-nudge`, …).
4. Do not commit `hookignore.yaml`.

Hooks already call `exitIfHookDisabled`. Do not delete hook scripts to silence them.
